The example registries, graph snapshots and demo identities under examples/
and docs/ are fixtures. The signing keys they contain are derived from
published seed strings (see `demoseed` in lib/common.sh) and are therefore
public and worthless; they exist so that a run reproduces byte for byte, and
must never be used to sign anything real.
